@startuml
title 46.1 y 46.2 - Listado y detalle de restricciones (ejemplo: zona restringida)

autonumber
hide footbox

actor "Frontend" as Frontend
boundary "API PROPUESTA\nGET /planning/restrictions" as API
control "Consulta propuesta\nNO IMPLEMENTADA" as Query
database "PostgreSQL\n(db_script.sql)" as DB

note over Frontend, DB
Contrato propuesto. No existe backend en este repositorio.
El listado ejemplifica restrictionType = RESTRICTED_AREA.
El detalle por ID es genérico y no filtra restriction_type.
end note

alt Listado 46.1
  Frontend -> API: GET /planning/restrictions?\ndistributorId=17&restrictionType=RESTRICTED_AREA&...
  API -> Query: validar query y paginación

  alt Query no interpretable
    Query --> API: BAD_REQUEST
    API --> Frontend: 400\n{success: false, code: 400, error}
  else Valor fuera del contrato
    Query --> API: VALIDATION_ERROR
    API --> Frontend: 422\n{success: false, code: 422, error}
  else Query válida
    Query -> DB: SELECT cabeceras FROM planning_restrictions\nWHERE distributor_id = :distributorId\nAND restriction_type = 'RESTRICTED_AREA'\nAND deleted_at IS NULL\n[effect, severity, is_active, search]\nORDER BY name, id LIMIT/OFFSET
    Query -> DB: COUNT(*) con los mismos filtros
    DB --> Query: filas + total
    Query --> API: proyección paginada
    API --> Frontend: 200\n{success: true, code: 200, data: {items, ...}}
  end
else Detalle 46.2
  Frontend -> API: GET /planning/restrictions/{restrictionId}
  API -> Query: validar restrictionId BIGINT positivo

  alt Path no válido
    Query --> API: BAD_REQUEST
    API --> Frontend: 400\n{success: false, code: 400, error}
  else Path válido
    Query -> DB: SELECT * FROM planning_restrictions\nWHERE id = :restrictionId\nAND deleted_at IS NULL\n(sin filtro por restriction_type)
    DB --> Query: cabecera o vacío

    alt Cabecera no encontrada
      Query --> API: RESTRICTION_NOT_FOUND
      API --> Frontend: 404\n{success: false, code: 404, error}
    else Cabecera encontrada
      Query -> DB: SELECT * FROM planning_restriction_schedules\nWHERE planning_restriction_id = :restrictionId\nAND deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY id
      DB --> Query: schedules[]
      Query -> DB: SELECT * FROM planning_restriction_vehicle_rules\nWHERE planning_restriction_id = :restrictionId\nAND deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY id
      DB --> Query: vehicleRules[]
      Query --> API: recurso canónico completo
      API --> Frontend: 200\n{success: true, code: 200, data}
    end
  end
end

note over Query, DB
No se consulta zones: sus filas son zonas logísticas de reparto.
El listado no inventa cityId ni scheduleSummary.
end note

@enduml
